WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.862 --> 00:00:04.136
- I can get this one
right, this is my brain

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:06.969
trying to take a fifth grade quiz.

00:00:10.316 --> 00:00:11.813
- I don't feel great about this.

00:00:11.813 --> 00:00:13.566
- I was actually born in Columbia.

00:00:13.566 --> 00:00:15.232
- I'm an adult, gotta pretty good handle

00:00:15.232 --> 00:00:17.400
on where stuff is in the world.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.293
- [Man] Which Great Lake
is the arrow pointing to?

00:00:22.293 --> 00:00:24.882
- Oh fuck. I don't know.

00:00:24.882 --> 00:00:26.633
- There are three (laughs), right?

00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:28.633
- That is Lake Michigan.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.718
- I'm just gonna say Lake Michigan

00:00:31.718 --> 00:00:33.430
'cause it's right near Michigan.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.020
- That's Lake Michigan.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.830
- There's not like one Great Lake?

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.697
- I wouldn't have gotten that,

00:00:37.697 --> 00:00:40.186
I'm not even gonna pretend
that I would've gotten that.

00:00:40.186 --> 00:00:43.019
Which city is not a state capital?

00:00:45.192 --> 00:00:47.693
- I'm going with Miami, Florida.

00:00:47.693 --> 00:00:50.026
- I think Miami is a state capital.

00:00:50.026 --> 00:00:51.830
- Miami, Florida is not a state capital.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.286
- Also like Miami can't be the capital,

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:55.847
I'm gonna say Miami.

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:57.936
- I figure it's too cool and neat

00:00:57.936 --> 00:00:59.423
to be an actual state capital.

00:00:59.423 --> 00:01:02.678
- [Woman] Which state is Wyoming?

00:01:02.678 --> 00:01:05.260
- The West is better because
states should be square

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.670
and 300 miles a side.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:10.062
- I should know this
'cause I like go to Wyoming

00:01:10.062 --> 00:01:11.645
every couple years.

00:01:14.865 --> 00:01:17.032
I don't think it's B or C.

00:01:18.872 --> 00:01:20.445
- I like the way that one's not angled,

00:01:20.445 --> 00:01:21.960
I think this one was
trying to throw me off.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.942
- The offset square, C.

00:01:23.942 --> 00:01:25.109
- That one, C.

00:01:26.012 --> 00:01:29.448
- Gonna say A, no last one
was A, see this is what I do.

00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:30.702
This one, D.

00:01:30.702 --> 00:01:31.535
- [Staff Member] C!

00:01:31.535 --> 00:01:33.108
- Son of a (grunts), I knew it.

00:01:33.108 --> 00:01:37.549
- [Man] Which state has more
coastline, Louisiana or Maine?

00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:39.917
- Maine is so small, no
Maine isn't that small,

00:01:39.917 --> 00:01:41.391
there's just not that many people in it.

00:01:41.391 --> 00:01:44.288
- I feel like Louisiana
would probably have

00:01:44.288 --> 00:01:45.833
more of a coastline.

00:01:45.833 --> 00:01:49.416
- I was just in Louisiana,
gonna say Maine.

00:01:50.491 --> 00:01:52.025
- I'm gonna say Maine.

00:01:52.025 --> 00:01:54.245
- I'm gonna go with Maine because

00:01:54.245 --> 00:01:57.409
Maine has probably more islands.

00:01:57.409 --> 00:01:58.936
- (laughs) Yes!

00:01:58.936 --> 00:02:00.393
- Guess that makes sense.

00:02:00.393 --> 00:02:02.104
- Jeez Louise.

00:02:02.104 --> 00:02:03.919
- What is the third smallest state?

00:02:03.919 --> 00:02:07.146
Is the most ridiculous
question I have ever heard.

00:02:07.146 --> 00:02:09.139
- Now is this by area or population?

00:02:09.139 --> 00:02:11.389
- Probably not Connecticut.

00:02:14.787 --> 00:02:18.135
- I know Rhode Island is pretty small.

00:02:18.135 --> 00:02:20.547
- Connecticut also seems
small, but maybe that's

00:02:20.547 --> 00:02:23.924
one of those secretly
big states like New York.

00:02:23.924 --> 00:02:26.594
- I mean I know California
and Texas are really big.

00:02:26.594 --> 00:02:28.064
- New Hampshire.

00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:29.339
- Vermont.

00:02:29.339 --> 00:02:31.152
- Is it New Jersey?

00:02:31.152 --> 00:02:33.150
- Connecticut?

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.341
It's Connecticut!

00:02:34.341 --> 00:02:35.404
(laughs)

00:02:35.404 --> 00:02:36.664
- I think Connecticut was big.

00:02:36.664 --> 00:02:37.997
- Yes, yes, yes!

00:02:41.271 --> 00:02:43.514
- Yeah that was an
enlightening experience.

00:02:43.514 --> 00:02:45.867
- Well, I got an F.

00:02:45.867 --> 00:02:49.049
- Spend the rest of the
day looking at a map.

00:02:49.049 --> 00:02:51.944
- It's too much pressure
to put on a fifth grader

00:02:51.944 --> 00:02:53.864
and a 29 year old.

00:02:53.864 --> 00:02:55.469
- Come tell me which rectangle is Wyoming.

00:02:55.469 --> 00:02:56.384
Do you know fifth grader?

00:02:56.384 --> 00:02:57.325
I don't think so.

00:02:57.325 --> 00:02:58.912
Have you been anywhere?

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.912
(upbeat jazz music)

